(CMMI Maturity Levels:) '
() '
(Level 1 - Initial:) '
(Processes are unpredictable, poorly controlled, and reactive. Work gets completed, but it frequently exceeds budget and schedule.) '
() '
(Level 2 - Managed:) '
(Processes are planned, performed, measured, and controlled at the project level. Requirements are managed, and processes are verified against project plans.) '
() '
(Level 3 - Defined:) '
(Processes are well characterized and understood, and are described in standards, procedures, tools, and methods. The organization's set of standard processes is established.) '
() '
(Level 4 - Quantitatively Managed:) '
(The organization and projects establish quantitative objectives for quality and process performance and use them as criteria in managing processes.) '
() '
(Level 5 - Optimizing:) '
(Continual process improvement based on a quantitative understanding of business objectives and performance needs. Focus is on innovation and technological transformation.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
